We don't need
infrastructure redundancy.

00:35:31.320 --> 00:35:34.470
Let's select an adequate
size for this one.

00:35:34.470 --> 00:35:45.040
A d2s_v4 should be adequate.

00:35:48.960 --> 00:35:51.900
And finally, username
and password

00:35:51.900 --> 00:35:53.130
for the administrative account.

00:35:53.130 --> 00:35:58.650
Let's just create a sample
administrative name, password,

00:35:58.650 --> 00:36:01.090
strong password, of course,

00:36:03.090 --> 00:36:06.930
and confirm that we have
an eligible license

00:36:06.930 --> 00:36:10.450
for Windows 11
available on hand.

00:36:14.400 --> 00:36:16.590
Let's launch the creation.

00:36:16.590 --> 00:36:19.930
It'll take a moment or
two to create the VM.

00:36:22.860 --> 00:36:27.600
Deploying a VM deploys
a lot of resources.

00:36:27.600 --> 00:36:31.260
And there we go, we are done.

00:36:31.260 --> 00:36:34.920
And now we've got our first
virtual machine deployed.

00:36:34.920 --> 00:36:39.000
It's already got the Azure
Monitoring Agent installed,

00:36:39.000 --> 00:36:41.940
so now we're ready to
connect it to Sentinel.

00:36:41.940 --> 00:36:44.800
Let's do that next.

00:36:46.700 --> 00:36:48.200
All right, back in Sentinel,

00:36:48.200 --> 00:36:51.620
let's now connect our
virtual machine to Sentinel

00:36:51.620 --> 00:36:55.610
so we can start receiving
security events.

00:36:55.610 --> 00:36:59.040
We're going to head down
to the Content Hub.

00:37:00.560 --> 00:37:04.310
And let's search for
Windows Security Events.

00:37:04.310 --> 00:37:06.510
Let's find the connector.

00:37:12.050 --> 00:37:12.800
There it is.

00:37:12.800 --> 00:37:15.200
It's already installed, but
it needs to be configured.

00:37:15.200 --> 00:37:17.610
Let's click on "Managed."

00:37:21.890 --> 00:37:23.150
And we're going to connect

00:37:23.150 --> 00:37:27.320
to our machine using Windows
Security Event via AMA,

00:37:27.320 --> 00:37:29.900
Azure Monitoring Agent.

00:37:29.900 --> 00:37:31.460
To do that, we're going to need

00:37:31.460 --> 00:37:35.480
to create a Data
Collection Rule, DCR.

00:37:35.480 --> 00:37:37.250
Let's go ahead and
do that right now.

00:37:37.250 --> 00:37:39.740
Create Data Collection Rule.

00:37:39.740 --> 00:37:42.330
We're going to give it a name.

00:37:43.650 --> 00:37:47.860
Let's just call it AZWinDCR.

00:37:49.890 --> 00:37:53.550
And the subscription, resource
group in which the machine

00:37:53.550 --> 00:37:56.340
and the DCR will exist.

00:37:56.340 --> 00:38:00.750
Next, which machine or
machines do we want to connect

00:38:00.750 --> 00:38:02.610
to this Data Connection Rule?

00:38:02.610 --> 00:38:07.860
In this case, we'll pick the VM
we've created just a moment ago.

00:38:07.860 --> 00:38:12.700
Collect. We're going to pick
up every security event.

00:38:14.670 --> 00:38:18.030
And next, create.

00:38:18.030 --> 00:38:21.120
We've set up our Data
Collection Rule.

00:38:21.120 --> 00:38:25.320
We've connected to the Azure
Monitoring Agent on that VM.

00:38:25.320 --> 00:38:29.880
Now, Sentinel can
receive telemetry

00:38:29.880 --> 00:38:32.410
from that virtual machine.

00:38:35.190 --> 00:38:38.880
If needs be, we can change
the Data Collection Rule,

00:38:38.880 --> 00:38:40.710
going back to the collector.

00:38:40.710 --> 00:38:42.360
But let's refresh, make sure

00:38:42.360 --> 00:38:46.470
that we can now see our
virtual machine in here.

00:38:46.470 --> 00:38:49.570
There's the rule
that we've created.

00:38:51.590 --> 00:38:54.830
Let's recap what we've covered
in this learning path.

00:38:54.830 --> 00:38:59.060
Microsoft Sentinel provides a
wide range of data connectors

00:38:59.060 --> 00:39:03.600
to bring in logs and alerts
from Microsoft services,

00:39:03.600 --> 00:39:07.320
Defender solution,
Windows Analytics host,

00:39:07.320 --> 00:39:11.520
third-party appliances, and
Threat Intelligence Source.

00:39:11.520 --> 00:39:16.320
We explored how Content Hub
solution bundles connectors,

00:39:16.320 --> 00:39:21.530
parsers, workbooks, analytics
rule, hunting queries,

00:39:21.530 --> 00:39:25.040
notebooks, watch
lists, and playbook.

00:39:25.040 --> 00:39:28.760
We also emphasized the role
of Data Collection Rule

00:39:28.760 --> 00:39:33.120
in managing collection at
scale, improving performance,

00:39:33.120 --> 00:39:35.070
and controlling costs.

00:39:35.070 --> 00:39:38.100
Finally, we looked at
how Threat Intelligence

00:39:38.100 --> 00:39:42.450
and Microsoft Defender
integration enhances detection

00:39:42.450 --> 00:39:48.330
and investigation capabilities
across the platform.

00:39:48.330 --> 00:39:50.460
This concludes our session.

00:39:50.460 --> 00:39:54.600
There are many ways to complete
your learning journey.

00:39:54.600 --> 00:39:59.790
We encourage you to watch other
videos in this course or search

00:39:59.790 --> 00:40:07.120
for your next favorite topic on
Microsoft Learn at aka.ms/learn.

